Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:11:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix screen-off audio stop on track change for USB direct
 playback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Fosi DS2 quirk changes caused the Rust audio engine to be recreated
on every track change (new signature per rate). The freshly-created USB
isochronous transfer threads need the CPU to stay awake, but no
PARTIAL_WAKE_LOCK was being held — the WAKE_LOCK permission was in the
manifest but unused. ExoPlayer/just_audio acquire their own wakelocks
internally; the custom Rust USB direct path does not.

The first track survived screen-off because the stream was already
stable. The second track died ~2s in because Doze throttled the CPU
enough to starve the new isochronous transfers.

Add a PARTIAL_WAKE_LOCK to MusicNotificationService, acquired when
isPlaying is true and released when playback stops or the service is
destroyed.

